{"anchor": {"begin": [31, 0, 246.67], "end": [31, 0, 420.67], "env": "lemma", "file": null, "head": null, "id": 9, "kind": "approximate", "label": null, "labels": [], "line": null, "number": "4.5", "source_sha256": "ea1fb5adf891158a69c49e13d1572ba7c7d9caae4b8259408a45cc2d7a437dd7", "statement": "Lemma 4.5. Let a > 0, b s ∈ R , and p s = (p s,1 , p s,2 ) ∈ R2 , and define t s , v s , P c , J c by (4.20). If v s > 2, the admissible stress cone condition, namely the inequalities in (4.21) together with v s > 2, is equivalent to P c > v s , (v s − 2)J 2 c < 2(P c − v s ) 2 . (4.22) For every nonempty compact set K ⊂ {(a, b s , w) ∈ R3 : a > 0} such that, for every (a, b s , w) ∈ K, a − b s w > 0, 2b s w + b 2 s a + (a − 2)w 2 < 2, there exists P K > 0 with the following property. For every (a, b s , w) ∈ K and every p s,1 ≥ P K , setting p s,2 = wp s,1 gives the relaxed cone condition (4.21). If also v s > 2, these data satisfy the admissible stress cone condition.", "title": null}, "blockers": [], "class": "proved", "clauses": [], "correspondence": {"by": "Christian Garry (drafted with Claude Code)", "confidence": "high", "coverage": "full", "note": "Split into the equivalence with (4.22) for v_s > 2 and the compact large-p_s,1 threshold for the relaxed and admissible cones.", "source": "confirmed"}, "decls": {"NavierStokes.ConeAlgebra.coneBound": "ea473a9666266858f91af5f9", "NavierStokes.SeedConePaper.AdmissibleCone": "6f33fd44101560ac750ea440", "NavierStokes.SeedConePaper.RelaxedCone": "37b61055d523cf642de534e4", "NavierStokes.SeedConePaper.parallelStress": "fe56b1ac17ac9df1036d8e9d", "NavierStokes.SeedConePaper.shearMagnitude": "ee103d43ec05412c09158f80", "NavierStokes.SeedConePaper.transverseStress": "9da7333a8f9e47428288d347"}, "findings": [], "heading": null, "id": "P:lemma-4.5", "key": "lemma-4.5", "kind": "lemma", "links": [{"axioms": ["propext", "Classical.choice", "Quot.sound"], "class": "proved", "doc": "The first assertion of `seed:cone-test`, in its origin